issible for this field, and the cited AX product is a bulk ingredient for animal drug compounding rather than a human antiseizure FDA label.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/cvm-updates/fda-grants-full-approval-drug-control-seizures-dogs-idiopathic-epilepsy","https://animaldrugsatfda.fda.gov/adafda/app/search/public/document/downloadFoi/17867"]},{"current_value":"Desitin Kaliumbromid DESITIN 850 mg Fachinformation (https://www.desitin.de/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Kaliumbromid-DESITIN-850-mg-Tabletten.pdf); FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"Kaliumbromid DESITIN 850 mg Fachinformation (German national Fachinformation; https://www.desitin.de/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Kaliumbromid-DESITIN-850-mg-Tabletten.pdf); PubMed PMID 31111774; PubMed PMID 22430156; FDA CVM KBroVet update; FDA Animal Drugs@FDA FOI Summary NADA 141-615","reason":"Replace the vague/disallowed DailyMed reference and add trusted FDA/PubMed sources for availability, aliases, and clinical context. Desitin supports many label facts but is not EMA/eMC/UK SmPC.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.desitin.de/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Kaliumbromid-DESITIN-850-mg-Tabletten.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31111774/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22430156/","https://www.fda.gov/animal-veterinary/cvm-updates/fda-grants-full-approval-drug-control-seizures-dogs-idiopathic-epilepsy","https://animaldrugsatfda.fda.gov/adafda/app/search/public/document/downloadFoi/17867"]},{"current_value":"EMA/UK SmPC","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"German national Fachinformation / manufacturer product information (not EMA/UK SmPC)","reason":"Corrects source-tier misclassification.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.desitin.de/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Kaliumbromid-DESITIN-850-mg-Tabletten.pdf"]}],"summary":"Needs update. Most German Fachinformation-derived dosing, formulation, metabolism, half-life, mechanism, and indication facts are supported, but the row uses an impermissible DailyMed boxed-warning source, overstates US non-availability by omitting 2026 FDA veterinary approval, misclassifies the mechanism source tier, and needs tighter adverse-event and alias/trade-name wording."}
